        <mxCell id="l7wsbRFqEFvn701YVKcY-44" parent="1" style="text;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="Raw CSV data is uploaded to the raw-file-pipeline S3 bucket, acting as the initial landing zone for incoming files.&#xa;&#xa;An EventBridge rule detects the file upload and triggers the AWS Step Functions workflow to begin orchestration.&#xa;&#xa;An AWS Lambda function is executed to perform preliminary data validation or metadata extraction.&#xa;&#xa;A CATCH block is configured to capture execution failures and send alert notifications via Amazon SNS.&#xa;&#xa;An AWS Glue Crawler is started to scan the data, infer the schema, and update the Glue Data Catalog.&#xa;&#xa;The AWS Glue Job is initiated to execute the primary Extract, Transform, and Load (ETL) logic.&#xa;&#xa;The Glue Job retrieves the data from the processed-file-pipeline S3 bucket to incorporate it into the current transformation task.&#xa;&#xa;The transformed data is written to the final-file-pipeline S3 bucket, partitioned by date and converted into the Parquet format.&#xa;&#xa;The end-user (Actor) performs SQL queries on the final dataset using Amazon Athena for analysis and reporting." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="271" width="759.25" x="-100.5" y="689" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
